      "side": 1,
      "message": "At the moment, `std::move` here doesn\u0027t actually help with performance because the current Builder functions don\u0027t ever take ownership of an input Vector. I think we could make it do so by adding an overload of `Values()` that accepts a `Vector\u003cValue*\u003e\u0026\u0026` that returns a std::move\u0027d version of the input vector. This should result in r-value constructors being called, such as in this case:\n```\n    template \u003ctypename... ARGS\u003e\n    ir::Construct* ConstructWithResult(ir::InstructionResult* result, ARGS\u0026\u0026... args) {\n        return Append(\n            ir.CreateInstruction\u003cir::Construct\u003e(result, Values(std::forward\u003cARGS\u003e(args)...)));\n    }\n```\n\nI\u0027ll still make the change so that in the future, if we fix this, we\u0027ll get the perf benefits.",
      "parentUuid": "0d869e86_f5790d33",
